@using System.Diagnostics
@using Showroom.Services
@inject CouncilWebData Data

@* The pre-registered test and its result, in plain words. The verdicts are shown as the files give them; a slope (beta) is never shown as a finding. *@
<section class="budget">
    <button type="button" class="check-head" @onclick="Toggle" aria-expanded="@(_open ? "true" : "false")">
        <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">@(_open ? "▾" : "▸")</span>
        <h2>Did the test find anything? No: it was inconclusive</h2>
    </button>
    <p class="plain">Before looking, a method was written down and committed: compare each council-year's file total with what the council declared to government, and ask whether the second copies the rules flag
        explain any of the gap. <a href="@DataUrl.For("council-web/PREREG_BUDGET_TEST.txt")" target="_blank" rel="noopener">The method as written before the run</a>.</p>
    @if (_open)
    {
        <div class="verdict">
            <p><b>In plain words.</b> The test was inconclusive, on every one of its arms. The flagged second copies are a median 0.01% of a council's file total (3.4% if the repeated-payment groups are added), while the ratio of file total to declared figure varies by about 23% between council-years (the comparator's own noise). A signal that small cannot be told apart from a gap that large, so the test cannot say whether any flagged row was an
                extra outgoing, and no slope from it is presented as a finding.</p>
            <p><b>The cities.</b> In Leeds the file total is between 11% below and 12% above the declared running expenses plus Housing Revenue Account, and 10% to 28% below once capital and pass-through payments are added.
                The second copies the test counts are zero in Leeds by its definition, so the test says nothing there, and the repeated-payment groups give a fit the pre-registration calls an unexpected shape, with no verdict
                (it reflects the size gap, not the flagged rows). The Leeds same-line-in-two-files repeats (£6.35m in 2022-23, £3.07m in 2023-24) are not in the statistic; they were found after the test was written.</p>
            <p><b>Four more cities.</b> In Sheffield, Bradford, Liverpool and Bristol the file total is below the declared running expenses plus capital and pass-through in all 17 city-years (0.56 to 0.99 of it), and the second
                copies the test counts are zero in Sheffield and 0.00 to 0.85% elsewhere. The test cannot tell whether flagged rows were extra outgoings. All six arms are inconclusive.</p>
            <p><b>Nine more councils.</b> In 49 of these 52 council-years (Wakefield, Coventry, Durham, Kirklees, Leicester, Cornwall, Nottingham, Wirral and Newcastle) the file total is below the declared running expenses plus capital and
                pass-through (0.45 to 1.84 of it, median 0.76); the second copies the test counts are 0.0% to 8.1% of the file total. All six arms are inconclusive: the test cannot tell whether flagged rows were extra outgoings.
                Pooled over all four groups the test now has 96 council-years, and every one of its six arms is still inconclusive. No slope is presented as a finding.</p>
            <p class="caption">Revenue Outturn is revenue only and net of recoverable VAT; this file is gross of payment, includes capital, pass-through payments, loan movements and credits. Employees are not paid through a supplier file.
                The published files cannot show which bank payments left.</p>
        </div>
        @if (_error is not null) { <p class="err">@_error</p> }
        else if (!_loaded) { <p class="hint">Loading the results (small files)...</p> }
        else
        {
            @foreach (var s in _sets)
            {
                <h3>@s.Title</h3>
                <table class="tests">
                    <thead><tr><th>Arm</th><th>Role</th><th>Council-years</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead>
                    <tbody>
                    @foreach (var r in s.Rows)
                    {
                        <tr><td>@r[0]</td><td>@r[1]</td><td>@r[2]</td><td>@Verdict(r[3])</td></tr>
                    }
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            }
            <p class="caption">Council-years in the first group: 19, from Reading, Bracknell Forest, RBWM and Merton. Wokingham's years are a worked example and are not in the test. Surrey, Essex, Hertfordshire, Stockport and York are in no group: no government figure is held here for them, so none of their years can be compared. Declared figures are the government's Open Government Licence statistics, credited by name and year on each council's page.</p>
        }
    }
</section>

@code {
    sealed class Set { public string Title = ""; public List<string[]> Rows = new(); }
    bool _open, _loaded;
    string? _error;
    readonly List<Set> _sets = new();

    static string Verdict(string v) => v == "INCONCLUSIVE" ? "Inconclusive" : v.StartsWith("UNEXPECTED SHAPE") ? "Unexpected shape, no verdict" : v;

    async Task Toggle()
    {
        _open = !_open;
        if (!_open || _loaded || _error is not null) return;
        var sw = Stopwatch.StartNew();
        try
        {
            var co = new Cooperative(CancellationToken.None);
            foreach (var (file, title) in new[] { ("budget_test", "First group (Reading, Bracknell Forest, RBWM, Merton)"), ("budget_test_stage2", "Second group (Leeds)"),
                         ("budget_test_stage2b", "Third group (Sheffield, Bradford, Liverpool, Bristol)"),
                         ("budget_test_stage2c", "Fourth group (Wakefield, Coventry, Durham, Kirklees, Leicester, Cornwall, Nottingham, Wirral, Newcastle)"),
                         ("budget_test_pooled_all", "First three groups pooled (44 council-years)"), ("budget_test_pooled_all2", "All four groups pooled (96 council-years)") })
            {
                var t = new Tab(await Data.TableAsync($"cross/{file}.csv", true, co));
                _sets.Add(new Set { Title = title, Rows = t.Rows.Select(r => new[] { t.G(r, "Arm"), t.G(r, "Role"), t.G(r, "Units"), t.G(r, "Verdict") }).ToList() });
            }
            _loaded = true;
            await Data.LogAsync("budget test built", sw.ElapsedMilliseconds);
        }
        catch (Exception ex) { _error = "Could not load the results: " + ex.Message; }
    }
}
